"toxic_monkey@hotmail.com" <toxic_monkey@hotmail.com> wrote:

> How do I take screenshots of NH?  I'm running it
> in Windows XP, using the text version, not the
> graphical version.

Pressing <shift><right-ALT><PrintScreen> does it for
me; that puts the current foreground window's bitmap
in the WinOS "clipboard". Then you can use any
application that can aquire graphics from the
clipboard. I use freeware tool "The GIMP"

http://www.gimp.org

but MS-Word and other MS image-aware tools work too,
and probably lots of other freeware tools as well.

The very nice freeware image display and
manipulation tool Irfanview

http://www.irfanview.com/

does the job slightly differently, it allows you to
set up a hot-key for screen or foreground window
capture (under its "options" menu) and specify that
the captured file pops up in the Irfanview tool for
further processing, or just is saved directly to a
file. This might be more convenient for grabbing
NetHack screenshots, as it could be done with just
a keystroke in the simplest case.

